---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ShareButtons from '../../../components/ShareButtons.astro';
import NextEpisodeTeaser from '../../../components/NextEpisodeTeaser.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Meta Muse Code: The Coding Agent Price War | Demystifying AI in 5 Minutes"
  description="Meta launched Muse Code, a terminal coding agent powered by Muse Spark 1.2. The Contributor tier costs $0.20/M output tokens, but Meta trains on your traffic. The price war for coding agents just went nuclear."
  image="/og-series-ep16-muse-code.png"
  keywords="Meta Muse Code, Muse Spark 1.2, Coding Agent, Terminal Agent, Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Price War, Contributor Tier, Async Subagents, AI Coding"
  publishedDate="2026-08-10"
  articleSection="Demystifying AI"
  articleTags={["Muse Code", "Meta", "Coding Agent", "Price War", "Muse Spark 1.2", "Terminal Agent"]}
>

  <style>
    .stat-card {
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }
    .stat-card:hover {
      transform: scale(1.02);
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.1);
    }
    .feature-card {
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }
    .feature-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    .tier-card {
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }
    .tier-card:hover {
      transform: scale(1.01);
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-border">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#06b6d4]/[0.04] via-background to-background"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top,rgba(6,182,212,0.06)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div>

    <div class="relative container-main max-w-4xl pt-20 pb-10">
      <a href="/series/demystifying-ai" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-secondary hover:text-[#06b6d4] transition-colors mb-8 font-mono">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"/></svg>
        cd ~/series/demystifying-ai
      </a>

      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
        <img src="/series/ep16-muse-code.png" alt="Meta Muse Code - The Coding Agent Price War" class="w-full h-auto block" />
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 md:gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[10px] text-[#06b6d4] font-mono bg-[#06b6d4]/5 border border-[#06b6d4]/20 px-2 py-1 rounded-full">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#06b6d4] animate-pulse"></span>
          EP 16
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1 text-[10px] font-mono bg-cyan/10 border border-cyan/20 text-cyan rounded-full">
          New Release
        </span>
        <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">Aug 10, 2026</span>
        <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">5 min</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground leading-tight mb-3">
        Meta Muse Code: The Coding Agent Price War Just Went Nuclear
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-secondary max-w-2xl mb-5">
        Meta launched a terminal coding agent that undercuts Claude Code and Codex by 21x. The catch? The cheapest tier feeds your code into Meta's training pipeline.
      </p>

      <ShareButtons title="Meta Muse Code: The Coding Agent Price War Just Went Nuclear" url="/series/demystifying-ai/muse-code" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Article Body -->
  <article class="container-main max-w-4xl py-8 md:py-10 overflow-hidden">

    <!-- TL;DR -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-4 md:p-6 mb-8 md:mb-10 max-w-3xl">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">// TL;DR</span>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-0">
        Meta shipped Muse Code on Aug 5, a terminal-only coding agent powered by Muse Spark 1.2. It scores <strong>82.9% on Terminal-Bench 2.1</strong> (vs Claude Opus 5 at 86.7%). The Standard tier runs $1.25/$4.25 per 1M tokens. The Contributor tier runs <strong>$0.10/$0.20 - but Meta trains on your traffic</strong>. First coding agent with persistent async subagents and crash-safe replay logs. Terminal-only, no IDE plugins.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: The Launch -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-mono text-sm">#</span> Mark Zuckerberg Enters the Chat
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Meta has been a spectator in the coding agent race. Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Grok Build - every major lab shipped a coding agent except Meta. That changed on August 5. <strong>Mark Zuckerberg personally announced Muse Code</strong>, a terminal-based coding agent that takes on "complete software engineering tasks across large repos."
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The pitch is not capabilities. Meta's own benchmarks show Muse Spark 1.2 <strong>trails Claude Opus 5 on every test it published</strong>. The pitch is price. And architecture.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-6">
        <div class="stat-card rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-3 text-center">
          <div class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">82.9%</div>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono mt-1">Terminal-Bench 2.1</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-3 text-center">
          <div class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">1M</div>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono mt-1">Context window</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-3 text-center">
          <div class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">1,000+</div>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono mt-1">Tool calls in 24h test</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-3 text-center">
          <div class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">$0.20</div>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono mt-1">Cheapest output/1M</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-[#161b22] p-4 md:p-5 overflow-x-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">ONE-LINE INSTALL</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-xs font-mono leading-relaxed"><span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">curl -fsSL</span> <span class="text-foreground">https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash</span>
<span class="text-secondary"># macOS and Linux only. No Windows. No IDE plugins.</span>
<span class="text-secondary"># Run `muse` in any project directory to start.</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: The Two-Tier Pricing -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-mono text-sm">#</span> Two Tiers: Privacy or Discount
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6">
        This is where it gets interesting. Meta offers Muse Spark 1.2 in two pricing tiers. Same model, same weights. <strong>The difference is what happens to your data.</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
        <div class="tier-card rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/30 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-4 md:p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#06b6d4]"></span>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">STANDARD TIER</span>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2 mb-4">
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Input</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-foreground">$1.25<span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-normal">/1M</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Cached input</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-foreground">$0.15<span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-normal">/1M</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Output</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-foreground">$4.25<span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-normal">/1M</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 mb-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-[#06b6d4] text-xs mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary"><strong class="text-[#06b6d4]">No training on your data</strong></span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-[#06b6d4] text-xs mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">3,000 RPM / 4M TPM</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-[#06b6d4] text-xs mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Enterprise-safe</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="tier-card rounded-xl border border-yellow-500/30 bg-yellow-500/[0.03] p-4 md:p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-yellow-400"></span>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-yellow-400 font-bold">CONTRIBUTOR TIER</span>
            <span class="px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[8px] font-mono bg-yellow-500/10 border border-yellow-500/20 text-yellow-400 rounded">DATA-FOR-DISCOUNT</span>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2 mb-4">
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Input</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-yellow-400">$0.10<span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-normal">/1M</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Cached input</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-yellow-400">$0.002<span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-normal">/1M</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">Output</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-yellow-400">$0.20<span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-normal">/1M</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 mb-0">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-yellow-400 text-xs mt-0.5">&#9888;</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary"><strong class="text-yellow-400">Meta trains on your traffic</strong></span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-yellow-400 text-xs mt-0.5">&#9888;</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">100 RPM / 3M TPM</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-yellow-400 text-xs mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary">12-21x cheaper than Standard</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The Contributor tier is <strong>21x cheaper on output tokens</strong> than Standard. That is not a rounding error. For a day-long coding session with 1,000+ tool calls, the cost difference is measured in hundreds of dollars.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        But the tradeoff is explicit: every prompt, every code snippet, every completion goes into <strong>Meta's training pipeline for future models</strong>. For open-source side projects, that might be fine. For proprietary codebases, that is a dealbreaker.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3: Benchmarks -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-mono text-sm">#</span> The Benchmarks Tell an Honest Story
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Give Meta credit for this: their own launch charts show Muse Spark 1.2 <strong>losing to Claude Opus 5 on every benchmark they published</strong>. No cherry-picking. No hidden fine print. Just second place across the board.
      </p>

      <!-- Desktop table -->
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border mb-6 hidden md:block">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-elevated">
              <th class="text-left p-3 text-[11px] font-mono text-secondary font-normal">Benchmark</th>
              <th class="text-center p-3 text-[11px] font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">Muse Spark 1.2</th>
              <th class="text-center p-3 text-[11px] font-mono text-secondary font-normal">Claude Opus 5</th>
              <th class="text-center p-3 text-[11px] font-mono text-secondary font-normal">GPT-5.6 Terra</th>
              <th class="text-center p-3 text-[11px] font-mono text-secondary font-normal">Grok 4.5</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-[11px] text-secondary">Terminal-Bench 2.1</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">82.9%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] font-bold text-foreground">86.7%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] text-secondary">81.8%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] text-secondary">81.6%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-[11px] text-secondary">DeepSWE v1.1</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">59.3%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] font-bold text-foreground">65.0%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] text-secondary">64.8%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] text-secondary">56.6%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-[11px] text-secondary">Meta Internal Bench</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">70.6%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] font-bold text-foreground">79.4%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] text-secondary">65.4%</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-center text-[11px] text-secondary">-</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Mobile cards -->
      <div class="space-y-3 mb-6 md:hidden">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-elevated p-4">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary block mb-2">Terminal-Bench 2.1</span>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <div>
              <span class="text-[10px] text-[#06b6d4] font-mono">Muse Spark 1.2</span>
              <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">82.9%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right">
              <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">Claude Opus 5</span>
              <div class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground">86.7%</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-elevated p-4">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary block mb-2">DeepSWE v1.1</span>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <div>
              <span class="text-[10px] text-[#06b6d4] font-mono">Muse Spark 1.2</span>
              <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">59.3%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right">
              <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">Claude Opus 5</span>
              <div class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground">65.0%</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-elevated p-4">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary block mb-2">Meta Internal Bench</span>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <div>
              <span class="text-[10px] text-[#06b6d4] font-mono">Muse Spark 1.2</span>
              <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#06b6d4]">70.6%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right">
              <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">Claude Opus 5</span>
              <div class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground">79.4%</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-yellow-500/20 bg-yellow-500/[0.03] p-4 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-yellow-400 font-bold">BENCHMARK ASTERISK</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-secondary mb-0">
          Every model was benchmarked inside its own co-trained agent (Muse Spark in Muse Code, Opus 5 in Claude Code, etc.). <strong>Artificial Analysis ran Terminal-Bench independently and got 80%, not 82.9%.</strong> Meta's previous model (Muse Spark 1.1) published 80.0% but verified at 76.2%. The gap between vendor-reported and independently verified scores is real and measurable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        On the <strong>Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index</strong>, Muse Spark 1.2 scores 54, tied with Grok 4.5. Claude Opus 5 leads at 61, followed by Claude Fable 5 at 60 and GPT-5.6 Sol at 59. Meta is not claiming the crown. It is claiming the price/performance ratio.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Architecture -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-mono text-sm">#</span> What Makes It Different
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Muse Code is not just "another CLI wrapper around an LLM." Three architectural decisions set it apart from Claude Code and Codex.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-4 md:p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#06b6d4]/20 border-2 border-[#06b6d4] flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <span class="text-[#06b6d4] text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">01</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold block">Persistent Async Subagents</span>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary">Background agents that outlive individual tasks</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-0">
          Claude Code spawns subagents per task. Muse Code's background agents <strong>stay active for the entire session</strong>. They avoid redundant context-gathering, take next steps autonomously, and decide when to report back. In testing, Meta had it build <strong>6 features for a game simultaneously with no collisions</strong> by fanning out to separate agents in isolated worktrees.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-4 md:p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#06b6d4]/20 border-2 border-[#06b6d4] flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <span class="text-[#06b6d4] text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">02</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold block">Crash-Safe Event Log</span>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary">Append-only log makes sessions replay-exact</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-0">
          Every model call, tool run, approval, and edit is appended to a local event log. The runtime is <strong>replay-exact and restart-safe</strong>. If Muse Code crashes during a 24-hour coding session, run <code class="text-[10px] bg-[#06b6d4]/10 text-[#06b6d4] px-1 rounded">muse resume</code> and it picks up exactly where it stopped. No lost work. No duplicate side effects.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#06b6d4]/20 bg-[#06b6d4]/[0.03] p-4 md:p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#06b6d4]/20 border-2 border-[#06b6d4] flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <span class="text-[#06b6d4] text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">03</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold block">Co-Trained Model + Agent</span>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary">Model and harness trained as a single unit</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-0">
          Meta did not slap a model into a generic agent harness. <strong>Muse Spark 1.2 was co-trained with Muse Code</strong> - including rejection-sampled harness trajectories, recipe optimizations for goals and compaction, and integration of the Muse Code toolset. The model and agent are designed to work as a pair.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-[#161b22] p-4 md:p-5 overflow-x-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">BUNDLED SKILLS</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-[10px] font-mono leading-relaxed"><span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">/plan</span>   <span class="text-secondary">- Produces an approval-gated plan before coding</span>
<span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">/grill</span>  <span class="text-secondary">- Stress-tests the plan until it holds</span>
<span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">/goal</span>   <span class="text-secondary">- Drives toward a stated objective</span>
<span class="text-secondary"></span>
<span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">muse</span>          <span class="text-secondary">- Interactive terminal session</span>
<span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">muse exec ""</span>  <span class="text-secondary">- Headless mode for CI/CD</span>
<span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-bold">muse resume</span>   <span class="text-secondary">- Resume crashed session from event log</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5: The Competitive Landscape -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[#06b6d4] font-mono text-sm">#</span> The Price War Landscape
      </h2>

