      <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Muse Code shipped fast, but it shipped incomplete. The gaps are not subtle.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-3 mb-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/20 bg-red-500/[0.03] p-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
            <span class="text-red-400 text-xs">&#10007;</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-foreground">No IDE plugins</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-secondary mb-0">
            Terminal-only. No VS Code, no Cursor, no JetBrains. Claude Code integrates everywhere. Codex has a web UI and cloud agents. <strong>Muse Code requires you to live in the terminal.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/20 bg-red-500/[0.03] p-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
            <span class="text-red-400 text-xs">&#10007;</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-foreground">No Windows support</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-secondary mb-0">
            macOS and Linux only. WSL2 reportedly works but is undocumented and unsupported. A significant portion of developers are excluded at launch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/20 bg-red-500/[0.03] p-4">
